{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg92ZPrZfw88MTiw731xw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the crash. All 17 tests pass (`python` isn't on this machine, so I ran them with `python3 -m pytest tests`).\n\n**Cause:** `Customer.discount_pct` holds a whole percent, so 10 means 10% off. `apply_discount` expects a fraction between 0 and 1, and `Invoice.line_total` passed the raw number. Any customer with a loyalty discount of 2% or more therefore raised `ValueError`. A 1% discount passed through but was treated as 100% off.\n\n**Fix:** In `shop/invoice.py`, `line_total` now passes `Decimal(self.customer.discount_pct) / 100`. I left the range check in `apply_discount` alone, since it exists to catch exactly this kind of mistake.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for a customer with a loyalty discount."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":23598,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":169},"output_tokens":279,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1191b488-df5f-4ce7-bb8e-940a4fb1fc05","uuid":"40ae73bd-9d6e-463c-ac98-3b4dba829e7f","timestamp":"2026-10-18T03:55:06.879Z","request_id":"req_011Cg92ZPaCCJNjPTQPBSYvZ"}
